<section class="detail-panel">
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 30 September 2026</p>
    <h2>How we review job listings</h2>
    <p>D2DJobs organizes opportunities from employer career pages, official recruitment notices, recruiters, and employer submissions. Before a listing qualifies for search indexing or advertising, our publishing checks require substantial role and eligibility details, skills, selection stages, a valid official source and application link, job-specific application steps, useful D2DJobs editorial guidance, and a source check recorded within the last 45 days. The automated checks measure completeness and freshness; an editor must still compare facts with the official source.</p>

    <h2>What we add</h2>
    <p>We structure the practical facts candidates need to compare opportunities: eligibility, experience, location, relevant skills, closing dates, selection steps, and how to apply. Each indexable listing must also include tailored application instructions and an original editorial note, such as role context, preparation pointers, or a useful point from the notice. We link to the source so readers can verify the opening and complete the application with the employer. We do not present copied third-party material as our own reporting or repeat one generic application paragraph across listings.</p>

    <h2>Incomplete or changing information</h2>
    <p>A listing that does not meet the publishing checks is excluded from job discovery and the sitemap, set to noindex, and does not display programmatic advertising. New incomplete submissions are held as inactive drafts. A source check older than 45 days no longer qualifies a listing for discovery until an editor checks it again and records the new date. Openings can change sooner, so candidates should always confirm details on the linked source before applying.</p>

    <h2>Employer submissions and paid placement</h2>
    <p>Employer-submitted jobs require administrative review before publication. Featured placement is clearly labelled and affects presentation only; payment does not guarantee publication or change our review standard. Browsing and applying remain free for job seekers.</p>

    <h2>Corrections and expired listings</h2>
    <p>Listings expire automatically 30 days after their source posting date, or their date added to D2DJobs when no source date is available. A supplied closing date can expire a listing sooner. The historical detail page returns a “Gone” status, is noindexed, has no application action or job-posting markup, and shows an expiry notice. If you find a closed role, broken link, incorrect requirement, or misleading detail, email <a href="mailto:contactsupport21@gmail.com?subject=D2DJobs%20listing%20correction">contactsupport21@gmail.com</a> with the listing URL and the correction. We will review the source and update, pause, or remove the listing as appropriate.</p>

    <h2>Editorial responsibility</h2>
    <p>D2DJobs is operated by Subash.G. Questions about these standards can be sent through the <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
</section>
